5,Romagnol — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Romagnol,"January 17, 2026 - The full classification tree is as follows: Indo-European > Italic > Latino-Faliscan > Romance > Italo-Western Romance > Gallo-Romance > Gallo-Italic > Emilian-Romagnol > Romagnol, distinguishing Romagnol from its western counterpart, Emilian, based on shared yet divergent evolutionary paths from Late Latin.[1][6] Key phonological features set Romagnol apart from Standard Italian, reflecting its Gallo-Italic heritage.",Romagnol,Indo-European
